issue.body:
Hello

I'm looking at an issue on the helm repository that use `jsonschema` since few months. [Users report errors](https://github.com/helm/helm/issues/31170) when dealing with external json file and URN. 

I tried to trick the json to load an external file using [FileLoader](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6#FileLoader) and then rely on this file as URN, like this:

```js
// main-fixed.json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema",

  "allOf": [
    { "$ref": "./external-conditions.json" }
  ],

  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "enabled": {
      "$ref": "urn:example:helm:schemas:v1:helm-schema-validation-conditions:v1#helmSchemaValidation-true"
    }
  }
}
```

```js
// external-conditions.json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema",
  "$id": "urn:example:helm:schemas:v1:helm-schema-validation-conditions:v1",
  "definitions": {
    "helmSchemaValidation_true": {
      "$id": "#helmSchemaValidation-true",
      "type": "boolean",
      "const": true,
      "description": "Value must be exactly true"
    }
  }
}
```

```sh
$ jv -o basic main-fixed.json 
schema main-fixed.json: failed
failing loading "urn:example:helm:schemas:v1:helm-schema-validation-conditions:v1": no URLLoader registered for "urn:example:helm:schemas:v1:helm-schema-validation-conditions:v1"
```

It seems only direct reference to the file, or including URN in the same json schema work but this tricks is not.

Feel free to close my issue if this is not something that you would want supported.
